From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:00:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/runtime: refuse a pipeline binary request that has no
 source

vkCreatePipelineBinariesKHR makes binaries from a pipeline, from keys and
data to import, or, on an implementation with an internal cache, from a
pipeline create info. When none applies, the function fell into the import
branch, whose only guard was an assert that a release build compiles out, and
dereferenced the import it does not have. A request names none when it has
no source at all, and also when it has only a pipeline create info on an
implementation without an internal cache, which has nothing to look the
create info up in.

Refuse such a request with VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED. The command defines
that result, and it is the one a command gives when the implementation
detects invalid usage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
index 8037fc4136149faab722f44727fc6d5dcc95175c..2fd9d8426c8a7660f1284a97da65993a675a3f33 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
@@ -4504,9 +4504,7 @@ vk_common_CreatePipelineBinariesKHR(
       default:
          UNREACHABLE("Unsupported pipeline");
       }
-   } else {
-      assert(pCreateInfo->pKeysAndDataInfo != NULL);
-
+   } else if (pCreateInfo->pKeysAndDataInfo != NULL) {
       for (uint32_t i = 0; i < pCreateInfo->pKeysAndDataInfo->binaryCount; i++) {
          vk_outarray_append_typed(VkPipelineBinaryKHR, &out, binary) {
             VkResult result = vk_create_pipeline_binary(
@@ -4523,6 +4521,14 @@ vk_common_CreatePipelineBinariesKHR(
             }
          }
       }
+   } else {
+      /* A pipeline create info alone is a source only where an internal
+       * cache looks it up, so a request can reach here with no source at
+       * all.  VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED is the result a command gives when
+       * the implementation detects invalid usage, and this command defines
+       * it. */
+      return vk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED,
+                       "a pipeline binary request has no source for its binaries");
    }
 
    return success_or_first_fail != VK_SUCCESS ?
